{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"long short term memory long short term memory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md","fileName":"Long Short-Term Memory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Long Short-Term Memory","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Recurrent Sequence Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recurrent Sequence Architecture","Recurrent Neural Network","LSTM Cell State","LSTM Forget Gate","LSTM Input Gate","LSTM Output Gate","aiassistants.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"long short term memory long short term memory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md","fileName":"Long Short-Term Memory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Long Short-Term Memory","heading":"Long Short-Term Memory","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Long short-term memory is a recurrent neural architecture whose gated memory controls what information is stored, exposed, or forgotten. The gates help useful signals persist across more sequence steps than in a basic [[Recurrent Neural Network]].\n\nLSTM networks became important for speech and language tasks because they can model dependencies that extend beyond adjacent sounds or words.\n\nIn Kelleher's account, an [[LSTM Cell State|internal cell state]] is carried forward separately from the immediate hidden output. A [[LSTM Forget Gate|forget gate]] filters previous memory; an [[LSTM Input Gate|input gate]] selects and adds new candidate information; and an [[LSTM Output Gate|output gate]] controls which parts of the updated state are revealed. Each gate uses ordinary neural units, so the LSTM is itself a small network whose controlled memory path reduces the training difficulty of basic recurrence.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recurrent Sequence Architecture","Recurrent Neural Network","LSTM Cell State","LSTM Forget Gate","LSTM Input Gate","LSTM Output Gate","aiassistants.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"long short term memory long short term memory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Long Short-Term Memory.md","fileName":"Long Short-Term Memory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Long Short-Term Memory","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiassistants.epub]]\n\n[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recurrent Sequence Architecture","Recurrent Neural Network","LSTM Cell State","LSTM Forget Gate","LSTM Input Gate","LSTM Output Gate","aiassistants.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}